  "body": "The design of 2026-11-05 (austin-org, org/org-development/process-study/hierarchy-ongoing-repeating-design-2026-11-05.md): a child carries a fit instead of appending to the parent's narrative; a leaf that gains a child is cut by the person (--core); ongoing tasks, closed by hand; after/due on any task with tsk when, local times stored with their UTC offset; ready's calendar sections; store format 2.",
  "types": [],
  "narrative": "Each child is one area of the design's section 3 (tool changes) and 4.5 (public documents), cut so that a reader can find a change by what it touches: the fit and the split, the ongoing lifecycle, the dates, the views, merge and format, the --by note, the documents; the last child is the release itself, carrying the release type. The ten end-to-end tests are owed by the children whose behaviour they name."
